{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1282690-the-secret-concord-what-have-you-done","id":1282690,"title":"The Secret Concord: What have you done?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-25T11:53:41-08:00","id":1282690,"title":"The Secret Concord: What have you done?","content":"So I run Boston Unveiled game and I lost a good thread that discussed a Blasphemous Scribe scenario with clauses to the Secret Concord. I figured the easiest thing to do is ask other seasoned vets what you have done with the Secret Concord.<br /> <br /> To give a concept of the style I have going is this. Think Mage Awakening and most CoD with meta plot of Vampire Masquerade V5. <br /> <br /> I personally took the Nemean stories and made his a type of &quot;Dark Knight&quot; tyrant. He sees how broken mages are and weak and how divided the Orders are and became a ruthless leader to unite them all in hopes he will make them all unite to one day overthrow hin. Like an abusive parent he puts his kids through hell so that one day when their ready they are mentally and emotionally strong enough to take on anything the world has to offer. He is the villian the Boston mages need to unite and he is ultimately sacrificing himself for them. <br /> <br /> Where I run into problems with the vague Nemean stories is ideas on the clauses of the Concord and who or what the 3rd party signatory is. Please describe what you've done.<br /> <br /> Here's a link to my Chronicle for fun <br /> <a href=\"https://mageawakeningbostonunveiled.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://mageawakeningbostonunveiled.obsidianportal.com</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25010,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25010-mrbishop","user":"MrBishop","date":". 01-25-2019, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25010-mrbishop","name":"MrBishop","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T13:37:54-08:00","id":1282712,"title":"","content":"My players haven't gotten to a point yet that the details really impinge on them but here's roughly what I'm running with:<br /> <br /> To start, Salem and the wider Massachusetts area have been touched irrevocably by the Chariot of Epona summoning the Prince of 100,000 Leaves. This centres on Salem, and accounts for why Awakened have traditionally stayed away, but it reaches out and touches people across the greater Boston area.<br /> <br /> The books says that the Putnams and Noose met at Salem, ready for war, but for some reason they made a treaty instead. Seeing as the Prince is an alternate timeline with some ability to mess with time more generally, I decided that it would make sense if the two cabals <i>did</i> go to war, but perhaps due to the resulting deaths and damage being too much, the remnants of the two cabals made a pact with each other and the Prince to erase their war out of existence.<br /> <br /> In return for the rewrite of time, the Prince will replace Boston at some point in the future. So, the cabals trade a rewrite for a destiny. The two cabals will cooperate to take the hierarchy of Boston, and then as the symbolic head of Boston, they'll hand over the city to the Prince. This is why there's a long break between the fall of the Emerald Scroll and the Noose-Putnam regime; they've tried to avoid their destiny as long as they can, but there are limits to what they can do because...<br /> <br /> Due to the rewriting of time, the only people with memories of what happened are the original signatories, and as part of the pact, they aren't able to speak about the details of the pact.. When these people die or leave, they are swapped out for a new signatory. Therefore, the leaders of the cabals have to deal with their cabal-mates without being able to tell them exactly what's going on.<br /> <br /> Or alternatively...<br /> <br /> The war between the Putnams and Noose reawakened the Prince (to the extent that you can anthropomorphise a sentient timeline). The two cabals essentially make the same pact as the first, but in this version, they're trading the immediate destruction of Boston (or maybe just Salem) for their cooperation in the future destruction of Boston (though with the presumptionthat they can find a way out).<br /> <br /> The first is the one I've had in my head, but writing this has made me think of a slight modification. The second makes it easier to justify why the cabals can't back out (it'd simply void the pact, and the Prince would take Boston).<br /> <br /> In either case, the Nemean has fallen into a bad situation. He may have wanted to play the Lion for the Boston Pentacle, but now he's read the Concord, he's fallen into a trap, (presumably, wherever the Stymphalian is, he's very happy to not have the responsibility anymore). In my thinking, the authoritarian style of leadership is the product of the Nemean wanting to control things as much as possible (above all, he needs to remain Hierarch), and it does do that, but only in the short-term. Long-term, he's building an ever longer list of enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","user":"Michael","date":". 01-25-2019, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T14:10:48-08:00","id":1282715,"title":"","content":"And that is a similar idea i have played with. My players are investigating that Epona and Putnams were at war for Salem when they awoke a part of the prince in the form of the Cannibals. Facing defeat a mage who knew about the scribe did a ritual summoning of a 3rd party, a Baron of the scribe. <br /> This Baron who is ultimately a Acamoth demigod servant to the Scribe agrees to wipe the cannibals from history in exchange for certain Clauses in a Concord. The clauses get more intense as it goes. One clause is that One mage will be the embodiment of the Secret Concord, should they be killed the killer inherits the knowledge of the concord otherwise it is passed on through ritual that will kill the host. <br /> In my story the Nemean killed the Symphalian in a duel for Heirarch and took on the burden to unite Boston. So based on vague meta from source books and other personal ideas what are more good clauses. Ideally Epona and Putnams gave opportunities for the prince to seep into reality if certain events of mage influence occured. The Nemean's secret goal other than preparing Boston mages to unite is to find a way to break or beat the clauses. One book teases that the 2nd clause is about to be set in motion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25010-mrbishop","name":"MrBishop","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T14:22:47-08:00","id":1282716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBishop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1282690-the-secret-concord-what-have-you-done?p=1282715#post1282715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my story the Nemean killed the Symphalian in a duel for Heirarch and took on the burden to unite Boston.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea. Might keep things a little cleaner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T15:10:55-08:00","id":1282729,"title":"","content":"Isn't the Nemean one of the signature characters in the 2nd ed book and a Scelesti?<br /> <br /> That night serve as as an escalation; he turns to the Abyssal powers to open options for his goals and to antagonise the people he wants to overthrow him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T15:43:11-08:00","id":1282734,"title":"","content":"So in Cage is a Lions Heart i used that as an astral dream journey for my players to discover there's more to the Nemean than he lets on. Books have teased that while his goals are noble to an extent power has corrupted him and he's very much struggling with his inner deamon, but in Lions Heart he discovers that his the younger self speaking to him is actually not his subconscious but a mysterious entity. In my story that entity is the Acamoth Baron which is why the Nemean was unable to speak the words of the concord. <br /> <br /> Once I have the various clauses down the final clause will result in the release of the Baron from the Concord into the fallen realm. &quot;Tarag&quot; as he will be known will then be free to personally unite the fragments of the prince scattered around the world to usher in the prince completely to this reality and replace it. <br /> Still stuck on what contractual clauses Epona and Putnams would bargain with the 3rd signatory about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25010-mrbishop","name":"MrBishop","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}